  "edge_schema": "ledgerloop_edge_saas",
  "prompt": "How quickly do users move through the month-end close funnel in the app, by the month in which they first uploaded a statement? A user starts the funnel at the user's first upload_statement event; event_ts is a UTC instant, and the month of that first upload is read in Brussels time. The user counts as matched in time with a match_transaction event at or after that first upload and at most 7 days (168 hours) after it, and as exported in time with an export_report event at or after the first such match and at most 7 days after that match. Return six columns, in this order: upload_month (the first day of the month), uploaded, matched_in_7_days, exported_in_7_days (each a number of users), match_rate (matched_in_7_days over uploaded) and export_rate (exported_in_7_days over matched_in_7_days), each rate a fraction between 0 and 1; export_rate is missing for a month with no user matched in time. Return one row for each month with a first upload. Any row order is fine.",
  "output_contract": {
    "columns": [
      {
        "name": "upload_month",
        "type_class": "temporal"
      },
      {
        "name": "uploaded",
        "type_class": "numeric"
